# TASK-010 — globally-locked dependency / environment paths override.
#
# Copy this file to `docs/plans/_global_lock_paths.yaml` (drop the
# `.example` suffix) to extend the default set declared in
# `plugins/plan-executor/scripts/plan_ops.py` (`GLOBAL_LOCK_PATHS` /
# `GLOBAL_LOCK_GLOBS`). The scheduler honors the override file if it
# exists and is well-formed; absence or malformed YAML falls back to
# defaults silently (a noisy override must NOT silently disable the
# default lock set — see plan_ops._effective_global_lock_set).
#
# Each entry under `additional:` may be either:
#   * a plain repo-relative path (treated as an exact match), or
#   * an fnmatch-style glob (any of `*`, `?`, `[`).
#
# Tasks whose `files` set intersects the effective union (defaults +
# additions) are batched alone — no parallel siblings, no other
# global-lock task in the same batch — to prevent silent races on
# environment-affecting state.
#
# Operator guidance: prefer adding paths over removing defaults. A
# false positive serializes one task; a false negative corrupts an
# environment.
additional:
  # - .env.example
  # - config/global.toml
  # - ci/pipelines/*.yml
